diff --git a/features/todo-completion.feature b/features/todo-completion.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..58acccb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-completion.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Feature: Todo completion and removal
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to mark todos done and clear them
+  So that I can manage what remains
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo marks it completed
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user checks the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed state
+    And the todo "Buy milk" has the "completed" class
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a single todo updates the mark-all checkbox
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user checks the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the mark-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Marking the last todo done checks the mark-all checkbox
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user checks the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user checks the todo "Walk dog"
+    Then the mark-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: The mark-all checkbox toggles every todo
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user checks the mark-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed state
+    And the todo "Walk dog" has the completed state
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed todos removes them
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user clears completed todos
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo titled "Walk dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button hides when no completed todos exist
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button shows when completed todos exist
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
diff --git a/features/todo-creation.feature b/features/todo-creation.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cee7886
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-creation.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Todo creation and list display
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to add and view todos
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+    Given the app is loaded
+    Then the new-todo input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Entering a title creates a new todo and clears the input
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: A blank title creates no todo
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "   " into the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list shows 0 todos
+
+  Scenario: No todos hides the main and footer sections
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows no items left with an empty list
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows one item left with a single active todo
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the plural count for several active todos
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..246de67
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to rename a todo in place
+  So that I can correct a task without recreating it
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters editing mode
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter updates the title
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user edits the todo to "Buy almond milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo titled "Buy almond milk"
+    And the todo "Buy almond milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur updates the title
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user edits the todo to "Buy almond milk" and blurs the field
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo titled "Buy almond milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing to an empty title destroys the todo
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user edits the todo to "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 0 todos
+
+  Scenario: Escape on an edit discards the change
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user edits the todo to "Buy almond milk" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a15b9e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want my todos to survive a reload
+  So that my list is not lost
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist to localStorage under the todos-vanilla key
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user enters "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    Then localStorage holds a "todos-vanilla" entry containing "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Reloading restores persisted todos
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk" already stored in localStorage
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo titled "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the app is loaded with the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user reloads the app
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/todo-routing.feature b/features/todo-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a319ad9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Todo routing and filtering
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed work
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only incomplete todos
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user navigates to the "active" route
+    Then the visible todo list shows 1 todo titled "Walk dog"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user navigates to the "completed" route
+    Then the visible todo list shows 1 todo titled "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Changing the route marks the selected filter link
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user navigates to the "active" route
+    Then the "active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The all route is the default selection
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the "all" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across a reload
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user navigates to the "active" route
+    And the user reloads the app
+    Then the "active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Checking an item in the active filter hides it
+    Given the app is loaded with the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And the user navigates to the "active" route
+    When the user checks the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the visible todo list shows 1 todo titled "Walk dog"
